{
    // Every weapon component vMenu knows how to offer.
    //
    // This is only a list of names. Which weapon accepts which component is asked of the game
    // itself when a weapon's menu is opened, so you never have to say. A component that no weapon
    // accepts simply never appears anywhere, and a weapon that accepts nothing just shows its other
    // options.
    //
    // The name on the left is the component's spawn name. The text on the right is what shows for
    // it, and follows the same rule as config/weapons.json: if it happens to be one of the game's
    // own label keys, such as "WCT_CLIP2", the game's translation is shown, so the menu follows the
    // player's language on its own. Anything else is shown exactly as you wrote it, which is what
    // components for addon weapons usually want.
    //
    // Components have no permissions of their own. Attaching one, removing one, and changing a
    // weapon's tint are all covered by the single permission
    // vMenu.Enhanced.Menus.WeaponOptions.Modify, so there is nothing here to grant one at a time.
    //
    // Listing the same component twice does nothing: the first one wins and the server console
    // tells you about it. Two different components are allowed to show the same text, which happens
    // a lot because most weapons call their own magazine "Extended Clip".
    //
    // These are read once when the server starts, so restart the resource after changing this file.

